# Figure 2 (kl-div 2a+2b): one Python-assembled 1x4 grid (PC/MLE, PC/MAP,
# GRaSP/MLE, GRaSP/MAP), sharing one legend above instead of each of the
# former 2a/2b panels drawing an identical n/linestyle legend row
# independently -- see plot_kl.py and palette.py's square_grid/
# add_shared_legend. One script, one PDF, included in the manuscript at
# native size (no \includegraphics width= -- see CLAUDE.md). Named for what
# it compares against (plain DAG-learning baselines: PC, GRaSP), paired
# with figure 3's kl_divergence_stagedtrees.pdf (staged-tree baselines) --
# not by figure number, which is a vestige that goes stale if the
# manuscript's figure order ever shifts (see kl_plot_stagedtrees's comment,
# the same reasoning that renamed that one away from "2c").
